values ('a4c8e2d6-7b19-4f05-9a31-3e0d6c5b8f17', 'motor-control-neural-control-of-movement', 'Motor Control / Neural Control of Movement', 'This course examines how the nervous system controls human movement. Students study nervous system organization, neural signaling, sensory integration, motor neurons and motor units, reflexes, central pattern generators, voluntary movement, cortical motor control, cerebellar and basal ganglia function, posture, balance, gait, neuromechanics, EMG and movement measurement, motor learning and plasticity, development, aging, fatigue, motor disorders, rehabilitation, sport performance, and applied case reasoning.');

