", "title": "Corticospinal tract"}, {"id": "2deca2bc-fd3f-42f5-aac0-0b6240fef139", "type": "concept", "title": "Reticulospinal tract"}, {"id": "71bc044d-0d6e-4708-8900-79d3245107bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Vestibulospinal tract"}, {"id": "a70b7115-37f5-4124-a40d-4b78875d744d", "type": "concept", "title": "Rubrospinal concepts"}]}, {"id": "0f05f0b3-7d92-4731-8869-6f92cffe94dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neural integration", "description": "Movement emerges from coordinated networks, not single command centers.", "children": [{"id": "992b1d16-a3af-41e6-a553-2e7d17357446", "type": "concept", "title": "Interneurons"}, {"id": "72bdf86c-2db1-45ca-8760-27100ce4df14", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergence and divergence"}, {"id": "4c5503ff-f69c-4f0d-bb03-09001edc5e74", "type": "concept", "title": "Recurrent inhibition"}, {"id": "b0ad53ed-288c-4a7a-9241-7133d55fd5a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Network-level control"}]}]}, {"id": "614598bc-c838-4901-be59-0ec78a3ef3a1", "type": "topic", "title": "Sensory Systems and Sensorimotor Integration", "description": "Explain how proprioceptive, vestibular, visual, tactile, and auditory information guide movement.", "children": [{"id": "6be03019-e8e4-4ee2-95d9-21dcd6e5261f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proprioception and somatosensation", "description": "Students learn how the body senses position, movement, force, and contact.", "children": [{"id": "b91d6c76-02f4-49b6-b327-2ddce7f86746", "type": "concept", "title": "Muscle spindles"}, {"id": "7fe5c5c0-1a6a-4435-905a-e3dc0a5c211a", "type": "concept", "title": "Golgi tendon organs"}, {"id": "d40abc44-2c6f-4260-b552-672c6377bc00", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint receptors"}, {"id": "6bae7f82-b708-4c30-8877-a3ef571e2953", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutaneous feedback"}]}, {"id": "e730e0cf-90f0-4623-af20-e445a50f839b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vision and vestibular input", "description": "Movement depends on multiple sensory frames of reference.", "children": [{"id": "286cda56-5539-4712-893d-a4fabefcfdaa", "type": "concept", "title": "Optic flow"}, {"id": "2e2a13e2-16cc-4123-b9a7-a589b8ae9107", "type": "concept", "title": "Gaze stabilization"}, {"id": "b8395c47-b1ee-4d9e-8b1f-a5fd2eddd2ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Vestibulo-ocular reflex"}, {"id": "12f3ec91-7aff-4578-9cdb-ac364b40156f", "type": "concept", "title": "Head position and acceleration"}]}, {"id": "968628f5-af7a-4bb1-b78f-5072089c095f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multisensory integration", "description": "Students learn how the nervous system weights information depending on task and environment.", "children": [{"id": "bafad892-e48f-4685-96c4-dc04643140f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensory reweighting"}, {"id": "74e42ad7-0aef-409b-a0a0-b33ff49ab05b", "type": "concept", "title": "Prediction and feedback"}, {"id": "78d6a04a-ac96-4cfe-8fbc-bd58fac90127", "type": "concept", "title": "Perturbations"}, {"id": "2fbe29d6-98ea-4e79-b16b-89826a4c9cf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Context-dependent control"}]}]}, {"id": "d1cbba3c-2ce4-414d-9c9d-e2d1eab5bf2b", "type": "topic", "title": "Motor Neurons, Motor Units, and Neuromuscular Control", "description": "Connect neural commands to muscle force, recruitment, rate coding, fatigue, and movement precision.", "children": [{"id": "64191f6c-d930-4dfc-8700-414897952ba3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motor units", "description": "Students connect motor neuron pools to force production and movement precision.", "children": [{"id": "dae5f1c7-5dea-46dc-81d8-a2d62f9682d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Alpha motor neurons"}, {"id": "67bdfc9e-b847-44a7-82be-2dda0fe05e4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor unit types"}, {"id": "35d178ca-db23-41cf-a908-c74d6096a549", "type": "concept", "title": "Recruitment order"}, {"id": "aed8d01a-609d-4a6b-817c-81b4378060ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Rate coding"}]}, {"id": "ee4a3244-68f6-48d9-a332-45563c10d60d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Force control", "description": "Students learn how neural strategies shape smooth, accurate, and powerful movement.", "children": [{"id": "8ba4a346-dd11-4b99-82a4-a8da0a59fc72", "type": "concept", "title": "Force gradation"}, {"id": "d58183b7-8126-47cd-ade1-75dbe61a44e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Coactivation"}, {"id": "b8daff5f-d45b-436f-b24d-9530b2821325", "type": "concept", "title": "Synergies"}, {"id": "5c00d252-c570-4d88-b04b-f4d9da8e4724", "type": "concept", "title": "Tremor and variability"}]}, {"id": "efa795b5-8c94-48e1-93df-ab0982130f70", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fatigue and adaptation", "description": "Students link neuromuscular physiology to performance and clinical limitations.", "children": [{"id": "62e65959-3957-4a37-b5aa-7667848a6d93", "type": "concept", "title": "Central fatigue"}, {"id": "b4fca046-e5ed-4232-9862-6665e24f47b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Peripheral fatigue"}, {"id": "48a89668-469c-4a6e-99b9-f5edc1ae80e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor unit firing changes"}, {"id": "7720addb-cefd-4e8b-9cd0-ff58a91dd920", "type": "concept", "title": "Training adaptations"}]}]}, {"id": "b69d9e20-6a62-4df1-9c62-bef56f86750b", "type": "topic", "title": "Spinal Reflexes, Central Pattern Generators, and Locomotion", "description": "Show how spinal circuits generate fast responses and rhythmic movement patterns.", "children": [{"id": "5ed90872-81c9-4e66-a8e0-f1e285729453", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflex circuits", "description": "Students learn why fast automatic responses matter for safety, posture, and coordination.", "children": [{"id": "193f1507-061a-48be-83f7-56d782c7b574", "type": "concept", "title": "Stretch reflex"}, {"id": "ad79ff34-67e7-401e-8da0-daaf886b25aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Golgi tendon reflex"}, {"id": "ffb193f7-d73b-4c52-85b3-cd0549d7338e", "type": "concept", "title": "Withdrawal reflex"}, {"id": "6b2a8200-93c7-47bb-a708-21c2315b7fee", "type": "concept", "title": "Reciprocal inhibition"}]}, {"id": "0626d600-4c70-4601-9159-0a4bbcf75bd6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Central pattern generators", "description": "Students explore how rhythmic movement can emerge from spinal circuits.", "children": [{"id": "fee14eb2-21e5-4eee-8ae4-75cec051fa4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Locomotor rhythms"}, {"id": "9afcf933-253c-40bb-8e1e-0b89e611ddf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexor-extensor alternation"}, {"id": "a5866ea0-ff24-4765-8f04-21727929f193", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensory modulation"}, {"id": "4943b8cf-4047-4721-b98f-9f25f86ef38a", "type": "concept", "title": "Animal and human evidence"}]}, {"id": "b4775f6d-0623-4ce1-bdc7-da672cd9ce7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Locomotor control", "description": "Walking is a blend of spinal rhythm, sensory feedback, and descending control.", "children": [{"id": "5457d55f-8b08-4f5c-9e50-715dbfa46f80", "type": "concept", "title": "Gait cycle"}, {"id": "a9d00703-aef9-457c-883c-e8bd189ce773", "type": "concept", "title": "Phase transitions"}, {"id": "8e95885b-bf95-4b0c-a378-08540513960a", "type": "concept", "title": "Perturbation responses"}, {"id": "d3378220-c69e-4403-9e92-0dca779aa16b", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation to terrain"}]}]}, {"id": "889ce49e-c5e9-414e-b948-bb4ab9823411", "type": "topic", "title": "Voluntary Movement Planning and Execution", "description": "Analyze how the nervous system selects, prepares, initiates, corrects, and stops voluntary actions.", "children": [{"id": "d46eff18-9093-4b1d-a7dc-cccc39991cf7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Action planning", "description": "Students learn how goals become movement plans before motion begins.", "children": [{"id": "128eb7a1-44fc-4c28-a9e4-a8a96d7ef207", "type": "concept", "title": "Intention"}, {"id": "dd8895c9-6d6b-4df4-adba-a9911e504387", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor planning"}, {"id": "8723e17c-7e6b-4e11-8b9a-7cd524cbbfb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Reaction time"}, {"id": "6bbf86c9-b487-4a5c-999b-5d3cc4f6cfbc", "type": "concept", "title": "Speed-accuracy tradeoff"}]}, {"id": "d8f5ee0